  "domain": "tier0/export/processing",
  "description": "Item 2.7 unrecorded paired discriminator for the arithmetic of a far tap's rigid turn (decision 364), the x90 twin of export-padding-turn-exact-x90 and export-padding-turn-exact-oblique: the world-offset probe's 3 flat convex seam pairs at their 123 copies (world offsets, 90-degree turns, 3D scales and UV-slot duplicates), the far island folded at exactly 90 degrees (J along (0, c, c)); both twins have the same layout, box anchors and UV slots, and the same UVs, band depths and 3D edge lengths, so a texel's pair is the same texel in the other twin; every position and UV exact in float32 and no two copies share a 3D point (tools/parity/fit/padding_turn_exact.py); predictions frozen before capture. User0-User7 added as RGB32F (a record whose template capture shows one of them not 32F is void); one fill with the eight channels active, Normal at opacity 1, default projection (read back), sources the authored float32 kernel code at the document size: User0-User2 one-hot the nine classes x mod 3 + 3 (y mod 3) of the texel (column x, row y from the top), User3 the UV ramp R = (x + 0.5)/N, G = (y + 0.5)/N, B = 0.5, User4 and User5 the periodic codes d and e (k/256, one 17 x 13 texel tile each), User6 (d + e)/2 and User7 1 - d. The eight maps at OpenEXR 32f with infinite padding and with passthrough (every covered texel must equal its source bit for bit, or the probe is void), every export step done twice in the session.",
